tools/mesa: the present probe (L39) -- one row per glXSwapBuffers

Why: "the window is black" was three different bugs wearing one screenshot.
(RimWorld L38: 3 of 3 runs reached the game loop, 8 flushes, no frame on the
desktop.)

  (a) the client never presents       -> no glXSwapBuffers, no XPutImage
  (b) it presents an unchanged or empty image -> "draws black"
  (c) it presents real pixels that never reach /dev/fb0 -> present plumbing

This tree's libGL is built from the gallium xlib frontend, NOT from src/glx
(there is no glxcmds.c object in obj/mesa/obj), so glXSwapBuffers here is
src/gallium/frontends/glx/xlib/glx_api.c: the hook has to live there.

glXSwapBuffers now calls the compat libX11's XcPresentMark() with the swap
count, the glFlush count (both counted here; _mesa_Flush is the other hook)
and the GLXDrawable.  The shim owns the XPutImage/XFlush counters and the
surface checksum and prints the [XSW] row, so the row exists even when the
swap hands XPutImage nothing.

The symbol is declared weak: against a real libX11 it resolves to NULL and the
probe costs one branch.  The first three swaps also print [XSWM] with the
resolved pointer and the XMesaBuffer, so "the client never swapped" and "the
hook is not bound" are different rows.

NOTE: this hunk deliberately sits at glXSwapBuffers and NOT at the include
block, because patch 0005 already owns that region; a block there makes 0005's
reverse-dry-run idempotency probe fail on an already-patched tree and the
next build refuses to apply it ("Reversed (or previously applied) patch
detected").

It also names a real defect on the way: XMesaSwapBuffers ->
xmesa_swap_st_framebuffer -> xmesa_st_framebuffer_display -> XPutImage, and
nothing in that path calls XFlush/XSync (only XMesaFlush does, and it is not
called by the swap).  A real Xlib writes the XPutImage request to the server
socket as it builds it; a compat Xlib that buffers the frame in its shadow
therefore never showed it.  XcPresentMark flushes the shadow it just filled.

--- a/src/gallium/frontends/glx/xlib/glx_api.c	2026-11-05 04:35:12.622765943 -0600
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/glx/xlib/glx_api.c	2026-11-05 04:35:12.624589727 -0600
@@ -1452,6 +1452,23 @@
 
 
 
+/*
+ * HOBBYOS (lane L39): the present probe.
+ *
+ * XcPresentMark lives in the compat libX11.so.6 (src/user/xcompat/libx11.c).
+ * It is WEAK on purpose: on a host build against a real libX11 the loader
+ * leaves it NULL and this probe costs one predictable branch.  It is what
+ * turns "the window is black" into three separable rows -- the swap count
+ * here, the XPutImage count in the shim, and a checksum of the surface the
+ * shim is holding.
+ */
+extern int XcPresentMark(Display *dpy, unsigned long long swaps,
+                         unsigned long long glflush, unsigned long drawable)
+   __attribute__((weak));
+static unsigned long long hobbyos_swap_count;
+/* Defined in src/mesa/main/context.c; the glFlush half of the same probe. */
+extern unsigned long long hobbyos_glflush_count;
+
 PUBLIC void
 glXSwapBuffers( Display *dpy, GLXDrawable drawable )
 {
@@ -1463,16 +1480,30 @@
       firsttime = 0;
    }
 
-   if (no_rast)
-      return;
+   hobbyos_swap_count++;
 
-   if (buffer) {
+   if (no_rast) {
+      /* Still a present attempt: the row must show that the client asked. */
+   }
+   else if (buffer) {
       XMesaSwapBuffers(buffer);
    }
    else if (os_get_option("MESA_DEBUG")) {
       _mesa_warning(NULL, "glXSwapBuffers: invalid drawable 0x%x\n",
                     (int) drawable);
    }
+
+   /* The row is written by the shim AFTER the put, so `put=` tells whether
+    * this swap handed XPutImage anything at all.  The first three swaps also
+    * print [XSWM] with the resolved pointer and the XMesaBuffer, so "the
+    * client never swapped" and "the hook is not bound" are different rows. */
+   if (hobbyos_swap_count <= 3)
+      fprintf(stderr, "[XSWM] n=%llu mark=%p drawable=0x%lx buffer=%p\n",
+              hobbyos_swap_count, (void *) (size_t) XcPresentMark,
+              (unsigned long) drawable, (void *) buffer);
+   if (XcPresentMark != NULL)
+      XcPresentMark(dpy, hobbyos_swap_count, hobbyos_glflush_count,
+                    (unsigned long) drawable);
 }
 
 
--- a/src/mesa/main/context.c	2026-11-05 04:35:12.623639603 -0600
+++ b/src/mesa/main/context.c	2026-11-05 04:35:12.625401039 -0600
@@ -1648,10 +1648,16 @@
  * Calls the #ASSERT_OUTSIDE_BEGIN_END_AND_FLUSH macro and the
  * dd_function_table::Flush driver callback, if not NULL.
  */
+/* HOBBYOS (L39): glFlush is part of the present probe -- a client that
+ * flushes but never swaps is a different bug from one that never flushes at
+ * all.  Read by the GLX frontend's XcPresentMark row. */
+unsigned long long hobbyos_glflush_count;
+
 void GLAPIENTRY
 _mesa_Flush(void)
 {
    GET_CURRENT_CONTEXT(ctx);
+   hobbyos_glflush_count++;
    ASSERT_OUTSIDE_BEGIN_END(ctx);
    _mesa_flush(ctx);
 }
